#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:118
msgid "A sample PLUMED input file"
msgstr "PLUMED 入力の例"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:120
msgid ""
"The main goal of PLUMED is to compute collective variables (or CVs), which "
"are complex descriptors of the system that can be used to describe the "
"conformational change of a protein or a chemical reaction. This can be done "
"either _on-the-fly_ during a molecular dynamics simulations or _a "
"posteriori_ on a pre-calculated trajectory using PLUMED as a post-processing"
" tool. In both cases, you should create an input file with a specific PLUMED"
" syntax. Have a look at the sample input file below:"
msgstr ""
"PLUMED の主な目的は、Collective Variables (CVs) の計算です。CV は系の複雑な記述子で、タンパク質の "
"Conformational Change や化学反応を記述できます。Molecular Dynamics 中に _On-the-fly_ "
"に計算することも、後処理ツールとして既存の Trajectory から _事後的に_ 計算することもできます。いずれも PLUMED "
"固有の構文で入力を作成します。次の例を見てください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:146
msgid ""
"In the input file above, each line defines a so-called action. In this "
"simple example, actions are used to compute a distance, a dihedral angle, or"
" print some values on a file. Each action supports a number of keywords, "
"whose value is specified. Action names are highlighted in green and, by "
"clicking on them, you can go to the corresponding page in the manual that "
"contains a detailed description of each keyword. Actions that support the "
"keyword `STRIDE` are those that determine how frequently things are done. "
"Notice that the default value for `STRIDE` is always 1. In the example "
"above, omitting `STRIDE` keywords the corresponding `COLVAR` files would "
"have been written for every frame of the analyzed trajectory. All the other "
"actions in the example above, i.e. DISTANCE and TORSION, do not support the "
"`STRIDE` keyword and are only calculated when requested. That is, `d` will "
"be computed every 10 frames, and `phi1` and `phi2` every 100 frames."
msgstr ""
"上の入力の各行は Action を定義します。この例では、距離や Dihedral Angle の計算、値のファイル出力を行います。各 Action "
"は複数の Keyword に対応し、値を指定できます。緑色の Action 名をクリックすると、各 Keyword "
"を詳しく説明したマニュアルに移動します。`STRIDE` に対応する Action は処理頻度を決めるもので、`STRIDE` "
"の既定値は常に1です。上の例で `STRIDE` を省略すると、`COLVAR` は解析する Trajectory の全 Frame "
"で出力されます。それ以外の DISTANCE と TORSION は `STRIDE` に対応せず、要求時だけ計算されます。したがって `d` は10 "
"Frame ごと、`phi1` と `phi2` は100 Frame ごとに計算されます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:148
msgid ""
"Variables should be given a name (in the example above, `d`, `phi1`, and "
"`phi2`), which is then used to refer to these variables in subsequent "
"actions, such as the PRINT command. A lists of atoms should be provided as "
"comma separated numbers, with no space."
msgstr ""
"変数には名前（上の例では `d`、`phi1`、`phi2`）を付け、PRINT など後続の Action "
"から参照します。原子の一覧は空白を入れず、番号を Comma で区切って指定します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:150
msgid ""
"You can find more information on the PLUMED syntax on the "
"[syntax](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-doc/html/_syntax.html) page "
"of the manual. The complete documentation for all the supported collective "
"variables can be found at the [page that introduces collective "
"variables](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/colvarintro.html)."
msgstr ""
"構文の詳細はマニュアルの [syntax](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/_syntax.html) を参照してください。対応する全 Collective Variables "
"のドキュメントは、[Collective Variables の紹介ページ](https://www.plumed.org/doc-"
"master/user-doc/html/colvarintro.html) にあります。"

