"the action TORSION and a set of 4 atoms. For residue `i`, the dihedral "
"$\\phi$ is defined by these atoms: C(i-1),N(i),CA(i),C(i) as shown in the "
"figure below:"
msgstr ""
"この機能で 5-HT1B Receptor の残基2の Backbone Dihedral Angle $\\phi$ (phi) "
"を計算しましょう。この CV は TORSION と4原子で定義します。残基 `i` の Dihedral $\\phi$ は、下図の "
"C(i-1),N(i),CA(i),C(i) で定義されます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:267
msgid ""
"![\"Definition of backbone dihedral angles, with dihedral phi highlighted in"
" red.\"](figures/masterclass-21-1-dih-fig.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Backbone Dihedral Angle の定義。phi を赤色で表示。](figures/masterclass-21-1-dih-"
"fig.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:269
msgid ""
"After consulting the manual and inspecting `5-HT1B.pdb`, let's define the "
"dihedral angle $\\phi$ of residue 2 in two different ways:"
msgstr "マニュアルと `5-HT1B.pdb` を確認し、残基2の Dihedral Angle $\\phi$ を2通りで定義してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:271
msgid "specifying an explicit list of 4 atoms (`t1`)."
msgstr "4原子の一覧を明示する方法 (`t1`)。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:272
msgid ""
"using the \\ref MOLINFO shortcut to select quadruplets for dihedral angles "
"(`t2`);"
msgstr "\\ref MOLINFO の Shortcut で Dihedral Angle の4原子を選ぶ方法 (`t2`)。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:288
msgid ""
"After completing the PLUMED input file above, let's use it to analyze the "
"trajectory `5-HT1B.xtc` using the driver tool:"
msgstr "入力を完成させ、driver で `5-HT1B.xtc` を解析してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:294
msgid ""
"You can modify the Jupyter notebook that you used for the first exercise to "
"visualize the trajectory of the two CVs calculated with the PLUMED input "
"file above and written in the `COLVAR` file. If you executed this exercise "
"correctly, these two trajectories should be identical."
msgstr ""
"演習1の Jupyter Notebook を変更し、上の入力で計算して `COLVAR` に出力した2つの CV の Trajectory "
"を可視化できます。正しく実行できていれば、2つは同じになるはずです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:297
msgid ""
"As a second example of MOLINFO's capabilities, we will use the advanced atom"
" selection tools provided by [MDAnalysis](https://www.mdanalysis.org) and "
"[MDTraj](https://mdtraj.org/1.9.4/index.html) libraries. Let's redo exercise"
" 1 above but this time use MOLINFO's shortcuts to select the CA atoms. You "
"need to complete the following template PLUMED input file using the "
"appropriate selection syntax for the corresponding library used. Please "
"consult the [MDAnalysis](https://www.mdanalysis.org) and "
"[MDTraj](https://mdtraj.org/1.9.4/index.html) documentation if you are not "
"familiar with these libraries and their syntax."
msgstr ""
"MOLINFO の2つ目の例として、[MDAnalysis](https://www.mdanalysis.org) と "
"[MDTraj](https://mdtraj.org/1.9.4/index.html) の高度な原子選択を使います。演習1をやり直し、今度は "
"MOLINFO の Shortcut で CA "
"原子を選んでください。使用するライブラリの構文で次の入力を完成させます。慣れていなければ、[MDAnalysis](https://www.mdanalysis.org)"
" と [MDTraj](https://mdtraj.org/1.9.4/index.html) のドキュメントを参照してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:316
msgid ""
"Now, you can compare the `COLVAR` file obtained with the one you obtained "
"when you completed exercise 1: they should be identical!"
msgstr "得られた `COLVAR` を演習1と比較してください。同じになるはずです！"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:318
msgid "Exercise 3: Using virtual atoms"
msgstr "演習3：Virtual Atom の使用"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:320
msgid ""
"Sometimes, when calculating a CV, you may not want to use the positions of a"
" number of atoms directly. Instead you may want to define a virtual atom "
"whose position is generated based on the positions of a collection of other "
"atoms. For example you might want to use the center of mass (COM) or the "
"geometric center (CENTER) of a group of atoms."
msgstr ""
"CV の計算で、原子の位置を直接使わず、ほかの原子群の位置から定める Virtual Atom を使いたい場合があります。例えば原子群の Center "
"of Mass (COM) や Geometric Center (CENTER) です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:322
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will learn how to specify virtual atoms and later use "
"them to define a CV. The objective is to calculate the distances between the"
" geometric center of the serotonin ligand (indicated as residue `LIG` in "
"`5-HT1B.pdb`) and the geometric centers of the two glycans located at "
"position N24 and N32. Glycans are carbohydrate-based polymers that are "
"sometimes linked to certain protein aminoacids. If you examine `5-HT1B.pdb`,"
" you will find the two glycans defined after the end of the protein, i.e. "
"after residue SER-390. These two glycans have different length:"
msgstr ""
"この演習では Virtual Atom を指定し、CV に使う方法を学びます。Serotonin Ligand（`5-HT1B.pdb` の残基 "
"`LIG`）の Geometric Center と、N24、N32 の2つの Glycan の Geometric Center "
"の距離を計算します。Glycan は、タンパク質の特定のアミノ酸に結合することがある糖質の Polymer です。`5-HT1B.pdb` "
"では、タンパク質の末尾 SER-390 の後に2つの Glycan があります。長さは異なります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:324
msgid ""
"the glycan attached at position N24 ranges from residue BGLC-1 to AFUC-9"
msgstr "N24 に付く Glycan は BGLC-1〜AFUC-9。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:325
msgid ""
"the glycan attached at position N32 ranges from residue BGLC-1 to AFUC-10"
msgstr "N32 に付く Glycan は BGLC-1〜AFUC-10。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:327
msgid ""
"Let's complete the PLUMED input file below. You can use the advanced "
"selection tools learned in exercise 2 to specify the atoms belonging to the "
"ligand and to the two glycans:"
msgstr "次の入力を完成させてください。演習2で学んだ選択ツールで、Ligand と2つの Glycan の原子を指定できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:347
msgid ""
"Once you have prepared a PLUMED input file containing the above "
"instructions, you can execute it on the trajectory `5-HT1B.xtc` by making "
"use of the following command:"
msgstr "上の指示を含む入力を用意したら、次のコマンドで `5-HT1B.xtc` に対して実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:353
msgid ""
"Let's now analyze the output of the calculation by plotting the time series "
"of the two CVs. Can you say if the ligand is overall staying closer to the "
"first or second glycan?"
msgstr ""
"2つの CV の時系列を描画して出力を解析しましょう。Ligand は全体として、1つ目と2つ目のどちらの Glycan に近いでしょうか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:355
msgid "Exercise 4: Fixing PBCs discontinuities"
msgstr "演習4：PBC による不連続の修正"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:357
msgid ""
"As mentioned above, `5-HT1B.xtc` is the raw trajectory generated by the "
"GROMACS MD code. Therefore, it typically presents discontinuities due to "
"PBCs. Many of the CVs used so far, such as CENTER or DISTANCE, take care of "
"these discontinuities automatically. However, other CVs need a special "
"command, called WHOLEMOLECULES, to fix PBCs discontinuities before the "
"calculation of the CV. In this exercise, you will learn how to use this "
"action."
msgstr ""
"前述のとおり、`5-HT1B.xtc` は GROMACS が生成した未処理の Trajectory で、通常 PBC "
"による不連続があります。CENTER や DISTANCE など、ここまでの多くの CV は自動的に処理しますが、ほかの CV は計算前に "
"WHOLEMOLECULES で修正する必要があります。この演習で使い方を学びます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:359
msgid ""
"We have seen that the first 40 N-terminal residues of the 5-HT1B receptor "
"are quite flexibile. In this exercise, we want to estimate the secondary "
"structure content (alpha-helix and beta-sheet) of this fragment during the "
"course of the MD simulations. In order to do so, we can use the following 3 "
"CVs:"
msgstr ""
"5-HT1B Receptor の N-terminal 側40残基は非常に柔軟でした。この演習では、その部分の MD 中の Secondary "
"Structure 含有量（Alpha-helix、Beta-sheet）を推定します。次の3つの CV が使えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:363
msgid "ALPHARMSD to measure the alpha-helical content of a protein structure."
msgstr "ALPHARMSD：タンパク質構造の Alpha-helix 含有量を測定。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:364
msgid "PARABETARMSD to measure the parallel beta-sheet content."
msgstr "PARABETARMSD：Parallel Beta-sheet 含有量を測定。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:365
msgid "ANTIBETARMSD to measure the antiparallel beta-sheet content."
msgstr "ANTIBETARMSD：Antiparallel Beta-sheet 含有量を測定。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:367
msgid "Let's first try to complete the following PLUMED input file:"
msgstr "まず次の入力を完成させてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:387
msgid ""
"and use it to analyze the trajectory `5-HT1B.xtc`. Can you say if the first "
"40 N-terminal residues tend to populate more alpha-helical or beta-sheet "
"conformations?"
msgstr ""
"これで `5-HT1B.xtc` を解析してください。N-terminal 側40残基は Alpha-helix と Beta-sheet "
"のどちらを多く取るでしょうか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:389
msgid "Exercise 5: Using RMSD to measure conformational changes"
msgstr "演習5：RMSD による Conformational Change の測定"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:391
msgid ""
"As previously mentioned, the first 40 N-terminal residues of the 5-HT1B "
"receptor are quite flexible, while the rest of the protein remains more "
"stable during the course of the simulation. In this exercise, you will learn"
" how to use RMSD to measure deviations from a reference structure. To use "
"this CV, you need to keep in mind that you must specify in the PLUMED input "
"a PDB file in which you mark the atoms that you want to use to:"
msgstr ""
"前述のとおり、5-HT1B Receptor の N-terminal 側40残基は柔軟ですが、残りは MD 中も比較的安定です。ここでは RMSD "
"で参照構造からのずれを測る方法を学びます。この CV には、次の用途の原子を示した PDB を PLUMED 入力で指定する必要があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:393
msgid "optimally align a conformation to the reference;"
msgstr "Conformation を参照に最適に重ね合わせる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:394
msgid ""
"calculate the displacement from the reference conformation after optimal "
"alignment."
msgstr "最適な重ね合わせ後に、参照 Conformation からの変位を計算する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:396
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that these two sets of atoms might be different! In fact, the "
"objective of this exercise is to calculate:"
msgstr "この2つの原子集合は異なっていてもかまいません。この演習では次を計算します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:398
msgid ""
"the RMSD of the backbone atoms of the first 40 N-terminal residues after "
"aligning the system on the backbone atoms of residues 41 to 390;"
msgstr "残基41〜390の Backbone 原子で重ね合わせた後の、N-terminal 側40残基の Backbone 原子の RMSD。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:399
msgid ""
"the RMSD of the backbone atoms of residues 41 to 390 after aligning the "
"system on the same set of atoms."
msgstr "残基41〜390の Backbone 原子で重ね合わせた後の、同じ原子集合の RMSD。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:401
msgid ""
"To create the two PDB files needed to define the two RMSD CVs, you can start"
" from the provided PDB file `5-HT1B.pdb`. Please consult the manual for the "
"RMSD action, in order to:"
msgstr ""
"2つの RMSD CV 用の PDB は、付属の `5-HT1B.pdb` を基に作れます。RMSD Action "
"のマニュアルを調べ、次を行ってください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:403
msgid ""
"create the PLUMED input file to calculate the two CVs defined above (use "
"`TYPE=OPTIMAL`);"
msgstr "上記2つの CV を計算する入力を作成する（`TYPE=OPTIMAL` を使う）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:404
msgid ""
"learn how to mark atoms for alignment and displacement in the PDB files;"
msgstr "PDB で重ね合わせ用・変位計算用の原子を指定する方法を学ぶ。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:405
msgid ""
"check whether PBCs are automatically taken care of or you need to use the "
"WHOLEMOLECULES action."
msgstr "PBC が自動処理されるか、WHOLEMOLECULES が必要か確認する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:407
msgid ""
"After analyzing `5-HT1B.xtc` with the driver tool, can you say which part of"
" the receptor is more flexible and deviates more from the starting "
"conformation during the course of the simulation?"
msgstr ""
"driver で `5-HT1B.xtc` を解析すると、Receptor のどの部分が柔軟で、初期 Conformation "
"から大きくずれるといえますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:409
msgid "Exercise 6: Aligning conformations to a template"
msgstr "演習6：Template への Conformation の重ね合わせ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:411
msgid ""
"In this exercise, we will learn how to align a MD trajectory to a reference "
"conformation, after fixing possible discontinuities due to PBCs. The goal is"
" to compute the vertical position of the serotonin ligand with respect to "
"the lipid bilayer. In the simulations of membrane proteins, typically the "
"initial conformation is oriented so that the lipid bilayer is parallel to "
"the xy plane (look for example at `5-HT1B.pdb`). Therefore, initially one "
"could use for example the coordinate `z` of the geometric center of the "
"ligand to measure how far it is from the membrane bilayer. However, during "
"the simulation:"
msgstr ""
"PBC による不連続を修正後、MD Trajectory を参照 Conformation に重ね合わせる方法を学びます。目的は、Lipid "
"Bilayer に対する Serotonin Ligand の垂直位置の計算です。Membrane Protein の MD では通常、Lipid "
"Bilayer が xy 平面に平行になるよう初期構造を配置します（`5-HT1B.pdb` を見てください）。そのため、初めは Ligand の "
"Geometric Center の `z` 座標などで Bilayer からの距離を測れます。ただしシミュレーション中には、"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:413
msgid "the system can translate from its original position;"
msgstr "系が元の位置から並進する場合があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:414
msgid "the system can be broken by PBCs;"
msgstr "PBC で系が分断される場合があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:416
msgid ""
"therefore one could not use an absolute position to keep track of the "
"location of the ligand. To solve this problem, there are several PLUMED "
"actions that can be used to make sure the system is not broken by PBCs, to "
"re-align it to a reference conformation, and thus to use absolute positions "
"safely."
msgstr ""
"したがって絶対位置で Ligand の場所を追跡することはできません。PLUMED には、PBC の分断を修正し、参照 Conformation "
"に重ね合わせ、安全に絶対位置を使うための Action があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:418
msgid ""
"To complete this exercise, the users will need to make heavy use of the "
"PLUMED [manual](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/colvarintro.html) to prepare the input file on their own. In the "
"following, some suggestions will be given:"
msgstr ""
"この演習では PLUMED の [マニュアル](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/colvarintro.html) を十分に使い、自分で入力を作成してください。以下にヒントを示します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:420
msgid ""
"first, make sure the entire protein is not broken by PBCs using "
"WHOLEMOLECULES;"
msgstr "まず WHOLEMOLECULES で、タンパク質全体の PBC による分断を修正する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:421
msgid ""
"then, make sure the ligand is not broken by PBCs and in the same cell as the"
" protein, using the WRAPAROUND action and the `GROUPBY` option;"
msgstr "WRAPAROUND と `GROUPBY` で Ligand の分断を修正し、タンパク質と同じ Cell に入れる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:422
msgid ""
"to align the _stable_ protein residues (as defined in exercise 5 above, i.e."
" residues 41 to 390) to the template `5-HT1B.pdb`, you can use "
"FIT_TO_TEMPLATE;"
msgstr "FIT_TO_TEMPLATE で、_安定な_ 残基（演習5の残基41〜390）を `5-HT1B.pdb` に重ね合わせる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:423
msgid ""
"at this point, you can safely define the position of the geometric center of"
" the ligand using the POSITION CV with the option `NOPBC`;"
msgstr "その後、POSITION CV と `NOPBC` で Ligand の Geometric Center の位置を安全に定義できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:424
msgid "the requested CV is the `z` component of the POSITION CV."
msgstr "求める CV は POSITION CV の `z` 成分。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:426
msgid ""
"You can check that your PLUMED input file is correct in two ways. First, you"
" can print out the conformations of the system after the transformations "
"done by WHOLEMOLECULES, WRAPAROUND, and FIT_TO_TEMPLATE by modifying your "
"input file as follows:"
msgstr ""
"入力が正しいかを2通りで確認できます。まず、次のように入力を変更し、WHOLEMOLECULES、WRAPAROUND、FIT_TO_TEMPLATE "
"による変換後の Conformation を出力します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:439
msgid ""
"Now, you can visualize the `5-HT1B_aligned.gro` file using "
"[VMD](https://www.ks.uiuc.edu/Research/vmd/). Second, if you inspect the "
"time series of your CV, this should be a continuous trajectory that spans "
"the range from 9 nm to 18 nm."
msgstr ""
"`5-HT1B_aligned.gro` を [VMD](https://www.ks.uiuc.edu/Research/vmd/) "
"で可視化できます。次に CV の時系列を確認し、9〜18 nm の範囲の連続した Trajectory になっているか確かめてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:441
msgid "Exercise 7: Estimating binding propensity"
msgstr "演習7：結合傾向の推定"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:443
msgid ""
"In this last exercise, we want to determine the propensity of the serotonin "
"ligand to bind the first 40 N-terminal flexible residues of the 5-HT1B "
"receptor and if there are hot-spots where binding is more favorite. In order"
" to answer to these questions, the user will:"
msgstr ""
"最後に、Serotonin Ligand が 5-HT1B Receptor の N-terminal 側の柔軟な40残基に結合する傾向と、結合しやすい"
" Hotspot の有無を調べます。そのために次を行います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:445
msgid ""
"compute the fraction of bound conformations over the total number of frames "
"in the MD trajectory;"
msgstr "MD Trajectory の全 Frame に対する結合 Conformation の割合を計算する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:446
msgid ""
"for each individual residue and glycan, compute the fraction of bound "
"conformation per residue/glycan;"
msgstr "各残基・Glycan について、結合 Conformation の割合を計算する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:447
msgid ""
"dump all bound conformations to a `gro` file, after fixing PBCs as in "
"exercise 6 above;"
msgstr "演習6と同様に PBC を修正し、すべての結合 Conformation を `gro` に出力する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:448
msgid ""
"for each individual residue and glycan, dump all bound conformations to a "
"separate `gro` file, after fixing PBCs."
msgstr "PBC を修正し、各残基・Glycan への結合 Conformation を別々の `gro` に出力する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:450
msgid ""
"To solve this exercise, no template PLUMED input file nor any indication of "
"the procedure to follow will be given. The users should only keep in mind "
"that:"
msgstr "この演習では入力のひな形や手順は示しません。次の点だけ考慮してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:452
msgid ""
"we arbitrarily define as *bound* a conformation in which at least one pair "
"of atoms of the ligand and of the protein/residue/glycan is closer than 0.4 "
"nm;"
msgstr ""
"Ligand とタンパク質・残基・Glycan の少なくとも1つの原子対の距離が0.4 nm 未満なら、*結合* Conformation "
"と便宜的に定義する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:453
msgid ""
"any pre-exisiting CV defined in the PLUMED "
"[manual](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-doc/html/colvarintro.html) can"
" be used;"
msgstr ""
"PLUMED の [マニュアル](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/colvarintro.html) にある任意の CV を使える。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:454
msgid ""
"any CV defined directly by the user in the PLUMED input file via the CUSTOM "
"action can be used."
msgstr "CUSTOM で入力内に自分で定義した任意の CV も使える。"
